{"id":"H3111","lemma":"יוֹיָדָע","transliteration":"yoyada","sayIt":"yo-ya-DA","language":"Hebrew","partOfSpeech":"","gloss":"Joiada","meaning":"A man living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at Neh.3.6;\nson of: Paseah (H6454I)\n§ Joiada or Jehoiada = \"Jehovah knows\"\n1) son of Paseah, who assisted to repair the old gate of Jerusalem\n2) son of the high priest Eliashib in the time of Nehemiah","glosses":["joiada","father of joiada","jehoiada"],"count":5,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"neh-3","v":6,"renderings":{"bsb":"by Joiada","kjv":"Jehoiada"}},{"chapterId":"neh-12","v":10,"renderings":{"bsb":"was the father of Joiada"}},{"chapterId":"neh-12","v":11,"renderings":{"bsb":"Joiada","kjv":"And Joiada"}},{"chapterId":"neh-12","v":22,"renderings":{"bsb":"Joiada","kjv":"Joiada"}},{"chapterId":"neh-13","v":28,"renderings":{"bsb":"of Jehoiada","kjv":"of Joiada"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"Nehemiah 3:6","note":"Joiada the son of Paseah and Meshullam the son of Besodeiah repaired the old gate. They laid its beams, and set up its doors, and its bolts, and its bars.","source":"web"}],"related":[{"id":"H3110","lemma":"יוֹחָנָן","transliteration":"yochanan","gloss":"Johanan"},{"id":"H0475","lemma":"אֶלְיָשִׁיב","transliteration":"elyashiv","gloss":"Eliashib"},{"id":"H6454","lemma":"פָּסֵחַ","transliteration":"paseach","gloss":"Paseah"},{"id":"H3129","lemma":"יוֹנָתָן","transliteration":"yonatan","gloss":"Jonathan"}],"senses":[{"id":"H3111H","gloss":"Joiada","relation":"H3111H ="}],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}